    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `customerCode` field formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` assigned on owner creation via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**What the code does:** when an owner is created, `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and `NNNN` = a 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (`findAll().size() + 1`), evaluated before the new owner is saved \u2014 so consecutive creates get consecutive numbers (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new) \u2014 OfficeFloor step that reads the built `@Val Owner`, computes the code, and mutates it in place.\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignCustomerCode` into the pipeline (after `applyRegistrationDate`, before `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`), so the count is read inside the same transaction just before the insert.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` response schema, which generates the field on `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table, and fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` positional seed inserts to include the extra column.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
